This product includes or builds on the following third-party work:

Models
- HuBERT Base (facebook/hubert-base-ls960), Apache-2.0, Meta AI. The v2 phone model
  is a fine-tuned derivative of it.
  Hsu et al., "HuBERT: Self-Supervised Speech Representation Learning by Masked
  Prediction of Hidden Units", IEEE/ACM TASLP 2021.
- Wav2Vec2 Base 960h (facebook/wav2vec2-base-960h), Apache-2.0, Meta AI. Used by the v1 pipeline.
  Baevski et al., "wav2vec 2.0", NeurIPS 2020.

Datasets (used for training and evaluation, not redistributed in this repository)
- LibriSpeech (train-clean-100, dev-clean, test-clean), CC BY 4.0.
  Panayotov, Chen, Povey, Khudanpur, "LibriSpeech: an ASR corpus based on public
  domain audio books", ICASSP 2015. https://www.openslr.org/12
- speechocean762, CC BY 4.0 (OpenSLR SLR101). Zhang et al., "speechocean762: An
  Open-Source Non-native English Speech Corpus For Pronunciation Assessment",
  Interspeech 2021. https://www.openslr.org/101

Software
- g2p_en (grapheme-to-phoneme), Apache-2.0, Kyubyong Park and Jongseok Kim.
- Scoring ideas follow GOP (Witt and Young, 2000) and GOPT (Gong et al., ICASSP 2022);
  the implementation in this repository is original.
- Full list of runtime dependencies: requirements.txt (each under its own license).
